schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: "Grassroots Economics' Sarafu Network scale (26,000+ people, ~290 communities)"
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    "Grassroots Economics reports the network has supported more than 26,000
    people across roughly 290 communities, with thousands now coordinating
    through Celo-based 'commitment pools.'"
  evidence: >-
    Attributed to Grassroots Economics' own Sarafu Network page, linked in
    the article's references — a self-reported figure by the project steward.
  source_lineage: "src/content/docs/what-is-blockchain.md — Grassroots Economics: Sarafu Network (https://www.grassrootseconomics.org/pages/sarafu-network)"
  interpretation: >-
    Used as the article's lead real-world example of blockchain-enabled
    community currency reaching people without smartphones (via USSD/basic
    phones), grounding the "trustless" and "immutable" concepts in a live
    deployment.
  uncertainty: >-
    Self-reported by the project steward (Grassroots Economics), not an
    independently audited figure; treat as the organization's own claim
    about its reach rather than third-party-verified impact data.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/what-is-blockchain.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
